On Wed, 10 Oct 2001 gwyllion@ace.ulyssis.org wrote:

> Hello,
>
> I just installed openbsd-snapshot on my DPW 500a (Miata) and everthing
> seems to work fine except the built-in DEC21043 ethernet.
>
> The NIC works (I'm on my network and everything works fine: I just
> download /usr/src and /usr/ports using anoncvs) but my syslog gets flooded
> by the following error messages:
> Oct 10 17:46:17 matrix /bsd: de0: link down: cable problem?
> Oct 10 17:46:45 matrix last message repeated 3 times
> Oct 10 17:49:09 matrix last message repeated 14 times
> Oct 10 17:59:12 matrix last message repeated 67 times
> Oct 10 18:09:14 matrix last message repeated 99 times
> Oct 10 18:11:15 matrix last message repeated 20 times
>
> When doing the complete opposite, actually unplugging the cable, I get the
> following message:
> de0: enabling 10baseT port
>
> I guess both messages are switched, due the fact this is an alpha
> architecture.

This problem is solved by using the dc driver instead of the de driver, as
suggested in some posts of the archive and by Nick Holland:
http://www.holland-consulting.net/tech/ocep/21143.html (OpenBSD Commonly
Encountered Problems: Using 21143-based NICs)

Everything is functioning correct now.

Wouldn't it be beter to make dc default over de?

Dries
-- 
Dries Schellekens
email: gwyllion@ulyssis.org

