I am certain isapnp is not quite cooked yet on alpha.   This can manifest
itself in various ways.  For example, while your card isn't even detected,
the floppy drive will be (when the kernel is built with the right options)
and the motor will spin but you'll get buffer overruns.  Another example
is the sb driver:  it won't even compile because there are header files
we haven't put in place yet.

This is good feedback, especially the note about the missing include for
the sb driver.  

When we have more of this complete, can I contact you to test again?

Jay


